        {
          "section": null,
          "text": "Program of Study",
          "codes": []
        },
        {
          "section": "Bachelor of Arts Degree Requirements for Sacred Music (Voice) Major:",
          "text": "Majors are given a diagnostic placement exam for both Theory & Analysis and Ear Training. If a student tests into MUS 100 and/or MUS 104, then those are required courses to enter Theory & Analysis I (MUS 109) and Ear Training I (MUS 107), respectively. However, MUS 100 and MUS 104 credits do not count toward the major.",
          "codes": [
            "MUS 100",
            "MUS 104",
            "MUS 107",
            "MUS 100",
            "MUS 104"
          ]
        },
        {
          "section": "Bachelor of Arts Degree Requirements for Sacred Music (Voice) Major:",
          "text": "Seven semester (21 credits) of primary instrument courses are required (MUS 172, MUS 173, MUS 272, MUS 273, MUS 372, MUS 373, MUS 472)",
          "codes": [
            "MUS 172",
            "MUS 173",
            "MUS 272",
            "MUS 273",
            "MUS 372",
            "MUS 373",
            "MUS 472"
          ]
        },
        {
          "section": "Bachelor of Arts Degree Requirements for Sacred Music (Voice) Major:",
          "text": "Four semesters (4 credits) of secondary instrument courses are required (MUS 174 / MUS 183). Note - Majors who have no prior keyboard skills may elect to take up to but not exceeding two credits of piano in preparation for organ study. Students with prior piano study and upon the recommendation of their professor must take organ for the four allotted credits.",
          "codes": [
            "MUS 174",
            "MUS 183"
          ]
        },
        {
          "section": "Additional Requirements:",
          "text": "Upon the establishment of a voice studio, weekly mandatory performance classes will be held. All majors are required to present a one-hour recital in their senior year.",
          "codes": []
        }
      ],
